reply.body:
I would rename `showContentNotSupported` to `showContentNotSupportedIfNeeded` and have it behave this way:
```java
if (!channelContentNotSupported || channelBinding == null) {
    return;
}
// all of the core currently in showContentNotSupported
```
Then it could be called both in `onViewCreated` (without the need for the `if`) and here just under `hannelContentNotSupported = true;`. This way we can be sure.

